  1. Everything except dapps/ and third_party/ — the daemon / consensus-execution
     core, the C99 crypto library (src/crypto), the light client (light/), the
     wallet (wallet/), the SDK and DSSO client libraries (sdk/), tools, tests and
     docs: Apache License 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). Free for everyone, for
     any use.

  2. All reference DApps (dapps/, D.1-D.9): Business Source License 1.1
     (LICENSES/BUSL-1.1.txt) — free for development, evaluation, testing and CI,
     and free for noncommercial production use by natural persons and
     noncommercial organizations; production use by or for a commercial entity or
     a government / public-sector body requires a paid grant
     (COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md). Each release converts to Apache-2.0 four years
     after its publication. The Licensor operates reference instances free of
     charge for end users.

  3. Vendored third-party code under third_party/ retains its own upstream license.

Per-file SPDX-License-Identifier headers are authoritative for any individual
file; the rule that assigns them is in LICENSING.md. Everything published through
2026-07-21 remains Apache-2.0 for its recipients; the BUSL tier applies to DApp
releases from v3.1 onward (forward-only, by the copyright holder).
